data: {"type":"chunk","content":"Grand Canyon in"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":" 3 days is a great window — enough time to actually settle in and do it right, wh"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":"ether that's rim walks and sunsets or a serious below-the-rim hike.\n\nBefore I l"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":"ock in the itinerary, I need two things that'll change the shape of this trip:\n\n1. **Who's going?** Solo"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":", couple, family with kids, bigger group — this affects trail picks and lodging.\n2. **Fitness level?"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":"** The Grand Canyon's biggest trap is underestimating the hike back U"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":"P. If you want to go below the rim (Bright Angel,"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":" South Kaibab), I need to know if you're comfortable with sustained steep clim"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":"bing in heat, or if you'd rather stick to rim trails and mule/"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":"shuttle viewpoints.\n\nOne quick note on logistics regardless of those answers: Grand Can"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":"yon doesn't currently have timed-entry requirements, which means no crowd control — South Rim parking lots ("}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":"especially Mather Point, Yavapai, Grand Canyon"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":" Village) fill up by mid-morning in summer. Plan to be at your"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":" first viewpoint before 7am or expect to shuttle/park-and-walk.\n\nI'd"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":" also default to basing you on the **South Rim** (Grand Canyon Village) since it's open"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":" year-round, has the most services, food, and lodging, and is the standard first-"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":"timer base — the North Rim is a solid alternative but adds a lot of driving (it's a 4-5"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":"hr drive around the canyon from the South Rim, not a quick hop)."}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":" Let me know if you specifically want North Rim instead.\n\nOnce I know group size and fitness level, I can build the"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":" actual day-by-day — heat management in August matters a lot for anything below"}

data: {"type":"chunk","content":" the rim (it regularly hits 100°F+ in the inner canyon)."}

